{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'winningTicketId|settlementComplete|WinningTicketMismatch|redeemWinningTicket|settleWinningTicket|clone|initialize' packages/contracts/src DESIGN.md WORKSPACE.md; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol | sed -n '90,220p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol | sed -n '1,100p'\"","aggregated_output":"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:17:/// @notice Atomically creates, funds, and registers autonomous fixed-implementation raffle clones.\npackages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:106:        raffle = Clones.clone(raffleImplementation);\npackages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:107:        // The fresh fixed-target clone can initialize only once; this function is nonReentrant and atomic.\npackages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:110:            .initialize(\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:22:        /// @notice The clone is initialized and waiting for the factory to escrow the configured prize.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:36:    /// @notice Complete clone-specific configuration supplied once by the canonical factory.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:184:    /// @notice Raised when a caller other than the immutable factory attempts clone initialization.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:286:    /// @param winningTicketId Previously settled winning ticket ID.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:287:    error WinningTicketMismatch(uint256 suppliedTicketId, uint256 winningTicketId);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:305:    /// @notice Initializes a fresh fixed-target clone with its immutable-per-raffle configuration.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:308:    function initialize(RaffleInitParams calldata params) external;\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:331:    function settleWinningTicket(uint256 ticketId) external returns (uint256 cashAmount);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:338:    function redeemWinningTicket(uint256 ticketId) external returns (uint256 cashAmount);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:406:    /// @notice Returns the immutable factory authorized to initialize this implementation's clones.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:500:    function winningTicketId() external view returns (uint256 ticketId);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:508:    function settlementComplete() external view returns (bool complete);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:518:    /// @notice Returns whether this implementation or clone has completed its one-time initialization step.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:519:    /// @return complete True for the locked implementation and every initialized clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:520:    function initialized() external view returns (bool complete);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:30:    /// @notice Emitted after a raffle clone is initialized, registered, funded, and active.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:32:    /// @param raffle Newly created fixed-target ERC-1167 clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:93:    /// @notice Raised when the exact configured prize is not owned by an active clone after escrow.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:94:    /// @param raffle Newly created clone expected to hold the prize and report `Active`.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:101:    /// @notice Creates, initializes, registers, and funds one autonomous fixed-target raffle clone atomically.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:103:    /// @return raffle Address of the newly created and activated clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:128:    /// @notice Returns the immutable implementation targeted by every registered ERC-1167 clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:138:    /// @return registered True only for a successfully created canonical clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:143:    /// @return raffle Registered clone address, or the zero address for an unknown identifier.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:24:///      owners burn them for redemption or refund. Each raffle is a fixed, non-upgradeable ERC-1167 clone with no\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:121:    uint256 public override winningTicketId;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:127:    bool public override settlementComplete;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:136:    bool public override initialized;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:153:    /// @param quoteToken_ Canonical six-decimal USDC contract fixed for the implementation and every clone.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:154:    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper fixed for the implementation and all clones.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:164:        initialized = true;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:176:    function initialize(RaffleInitParams calldata params) external override {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:177:        if (initialized) revert AlreadyInitialized();\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:179:        initialized = true;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304:    function settleWinningTicket(uint256 ticketId) external override nonReentrant returns (uint256 cashAmount) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305:        cashAmount = _settleWinningTicket(ticketId);\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:309:    function redeemWinningTicket(uint256 ticketId) external override nonReentrant returns (uint256 cashAmount) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:314:        if (!settlementComplete) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:315:            _settleWinningTicket(ticketId);\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:316:        } else if (ticketId != winningTicketId) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:317:            revert WinningTicketMismatch(ticketId, winningTicketId);\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:533:    function _settleWinningTicket(uint256 ticketId) private returns (uint256 cashAmount) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534:        if (settlementComplete) revert SettlementAlreadyComplete();\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:551:        settlementComplete = true;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:552:        winningTicketId = ticketId;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:588:    ///      Initialization supplies the prospective prize token because clone storage is not populated yet; runtime\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:607:    /// @dev Validates the wrapper before passing it to the inherited constructor initializer.\nDESIGN.md:2:Ethereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\n    90\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == implementation) revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    91\t        raffleImplementation = implementation;\n    92\t    }\n    93\t\n    94\t    // External state-changing functions\n    95\t\n    96\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    97\t    function createRaffle(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) external override nonReentrant returns (address raffle) {\n    98\t        _validateCreateParams(params);\n    99\t        uint256 currentTime = block.timestamp;\n   100\t        if (params.endTime <= currentTime) revert InvalidEndTime(currentTime, params.endTime);\n   101\t        uint256 saleDuration = uint256(params.endTime) - currentTime;\n   102\t        if (saleDuration > RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION) {\n   103\t            revert SaleDurationTooLong(saleDuration, RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION);\n   104\t        }\n   105\t        uint256 raffleId = ++raffleCount;\n   106\t        raffle = Clones.clone(raffleImplementation);\n   107\t        // The fresh fixed-target clone can initialize only once; this function is nonReentrant and atomic.\n   108\t        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-no-eth\n   109\t        IRaffle(raffle)\n   110\t            .initialize(\n   111\t                IRaffle.RaffleInitParams({\n   112\t                sponsor: msg.sender,\n   113\t                sponsorRecipient: params.sponsorRecipient,\n   114\t                protocolTreasury: protocolTreasury,\n   115\t                prizeToken: params.prizeToken,\n   116\t                prizeTokenId: params.prizeTokenId,\n   117\t                raffleId: raffleId,\n   118\t                reserveEntries: params.reserveEntries,\n   119\t                endTime: params.endTime\n   120\t            })\n   121\t            );\n   122\t\n   123\t        raffleById[raffleId] = raffle;\n   124\t        idByRaffle[raffle] = raffleId;\n   125\t        isRaffle[raffle] = true;\n   126\t\n   127\t        IERC721 prize = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\n   128\t        prize.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, raffle, params.prizeTokenId);\n   129\t        if (prize.ownerOf(params.prizeTokenId) != raffle) {\n   130\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   131\t        }\n   132\t        if (IRaffle(raffle).status() != IRaffle.Status.Active) {\n   133\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   134\t        }\n   135\t\n   136\t        emit RaffleCreated(\n   137\t            raffleId,\n   138\t            raffle,\n   139\t            msg.sender,\n   140\t            params.sponsorRecipient,\n   141\t            params.prizeToken,\n   142\t            params.prizeTokenId,\n   143\t            quoteToken,\n   144\t            protocolTreasury,\n   145\t            params.reserveEntries,\n   146\t            params.endTime\n   147\t        );\n   148\t    }\n   149\t\n   150\t    // Private view helpers\n   151\t\n   152\t    /// @dev Validates the sponsor-selected token, recipient, reserve, and supported ERC-721 interface before cloning.\n   153\t    /// @param params Prospective raffle configuration supplied by the sponsor.\n   154\t    function _validateCreateParams(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) private view {\n   155\t        _requireContract(params.prizeToken);\n   156\t        if (params.sponsorRecipient == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n   157\t        if (\n   158\t            params.prizeToken == address(this) || params.prizeToken == quoteToken || params.prizeToken == vrfWrapper\n   159\t                || params.prizeToken == raffleImplementation || isRaffle[params.prizeToken]\n   160\t        ) {\n   161\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.prizeToken);\n   162\t        }\n   163\t        if (\n   164\t            params.sponsorRecipient == address(this) || params.sponsorRecipient == quoteToken\n   165\t                || params.sponsorRecipient == vrfWrapper || params.sponsorRecipient == params.prizeToken\n   166\t                || params.sponsorRecipient == raffleImplementation || isRaffle[params.sponsorRecipient]\n   167\t        ) {\n   168\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.sponsorRecipient);\n   169\t        }\n   170\t\n   171\t        bool supports721 = false;\n   172\t        try IERC165(params.prizeToken).supportsInterface(type(IERC721).interfaceId) returns (bool supported) {\n   173\t            supports721 = supported;\n   174\t        } catch {\n   175\t            revert UnsupportedPrizeToken(params.prizeToken);\n   176\t        }\n   177\t        if (!supports721) revert UnsupportedPrizeToken(params.prizeToken);\n   178\t        if (params.reserveEntries == 0) revert ZeroReserveEntries();\n   179\t    }\n   180\t\n   181\t    /// @dev Reverts unless an address contains deployed code.\n   182\t    /// @param account Address required to be a contract.\n   183\t    function _requireContract(address account) private view {\n   184\t        if (account.code.length == 0) revert NotContract(account);\n   185\t    }\n   186\t}\n     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\tpragma solidity 0.8.36;\n     3\t\n     4\timport { IVRFV2PlusWrapper } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol\";\n     5\timport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n     6\timport { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n     7\t\n     8\t/// @title raffle.fun Raffle Interface\n     9\t/// @author heesho\n    10\t/// @notice Defines one autonomous NFT raffle using fixed-price USDC entries and one transferable ERC-721 ticket per\n    11\t///         purchase.\n    12\t/// @dev Ticket IDs are sequential. Each ticket stores one inclusive uint128 entry range and remains a transferable\n    13\t///      bearer claim until its owner atomically burns it for redemption or refund. The immutable quote token is trusted\n    14\t///      canonical six-decimal USDC with standard, non-rebasing, fee-free transfers. Supported prizes are honest,\n    15\t///      standards-compliant ERC-721s.\n    16\t/// @custom:version 1.0.0\n    17\tinterface IRaffle {\n    18\t    // Types\n    19\t\n    20\t    /// @notice The single authoritative raffle lifecycle and economic result.\n    21\t    enum Status {\n    22\t        /// @notice The clone is initialized and waiting for the factory to escrow the configured prize.\n    23\t        AwaitingPrize,\n    24\t        /// @notice The prize is escrowed and entry sales or post-sale draw initiation are available.\n    25\t        Active,\n    26\t        /// @notice A Chainlink VRF request was accepted and its callback window is open.\n    27\t        Drawing,\n    28\t        /// @notice The reserve was met and the winning ticket may redeem the prize NFT.\n    29\t        NftWon,\n    30\t        /// @notice The reserve was missed and the winning ticket may redeem its cash allocation.\n    31\t        CashWon,\n    32\t        /// @notice Full ticket refunds are enabled and the sponsor may recover the prize NFT.\n    33\t        Refunding\n    34\t    }\n    35\t\n    36\t    /// @notice Complete clone-specific configuration supplied once by the canonical factory.\n    37\t    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and empty-raffle cancellation authority.\n    38\t    /// @param sponsorRecipient Immutable recipient of sponsor quote proceeds and any returned prize.\n    39\t    /// @param protocolTreasury Immutable recipient of protocol fees.\n    40\t    /// @param prizeToken Standards-compliant ERC-721 prize contract.\n    41\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the prize escrowed by this raffle.\n    42\t    /// @param raffleId One-based canonical factory identifier for this raffle.\n    43\t    /// @param reserveEntries Global raw entry-count threshold selecting the NFT outcome when met or exceeded.\n    44\t    /// @param endTime Unix timestamp, in seconds, at which entry sales end exclusively.\n    45\t    struct RaffleInitParams {\n    46\t        address sponsor;\n    47\t        address sponsorRecipient;\n    48\t        address protocolTreasury;\n    49\t        address prizeToken;\n    50\t        uint256 prizeTokenId;\n    51\t        uint256 raffleId;\n    52\t        uint128 reserveEntries;\n    53\t        uint64 endTime;\n    54\t    }\n    55\t\n    56\t    // Events\n    57\t\n    58\t    /// @notice Emitted when the factory deposits the configured prize and activates the raffle.\n    59\t    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 contract of the deposited prize.\n    60\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the deposited prize.\n    61\t    /// @param sponsor Address that deposited the prize through the factory.\n    62\t    event PrizeDeposited(address indexed prizeToken, uint256 indexed prizeTokenId, address indexed sponsor);\n    63\t\n    64\t    /// @notice Emitted when a buyer pays for entries and one range ticket is minted.\n    65\t    /// @param buyer Address that paid the six-decimal quote-token amount.\n    66\t    /// @param recipient Address that received the newly minted ticket.\n    67\t    /// @param ticketId Sequential ticket ID assigned to the purchase.\n    68\t    /// @param firstEntry First global raffle entry represented by the ticket, inclusive.\n    69\t    /// @param lastEntry Last global raffle entry represented by the ticket, inclusive.\n    70\t    /// @param entryCount Number of entries represented by the ticket.\n    71\t    /// @param grossAmount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid, equal to `entryCount * ENTRY_PRICE`.\n    72\t    event TicketPurchased(\n    73\t        address indexed buyer,\n    74\t        address indexed recipient,\n    75\t        uint256 indexed ticketId,\n    76\t        uint128 firstEntry,\n    77\t        uint128 lastEntry,\n    78\t        uint128 entryCount,\n    79\t        uint256 grossAmount\n    80\t    );\n    81\t\n    82\t    /// @notice Emitted when the raffle pays for and records its one Chainlink VRF request.\n    83\t    /// @param requestId Wrapper-assigned request identifier.\n    84\t    /// @param requester Address that initiated and funded the request.\n    85\t    /// @param fee Native-token wei actually paid to the wrapper for the request.\n    86\t    /// @param excessReturned Native-token wei returned to the requester after paying the actual fee.\n    87\t    /// @param drawRequestedAt Unix timestamp, in seconds, when the request was accepted.\n    88\t    /// @param callbackDeadline Exclusive Unix-timestamp deadline for accepting the authenticated callback.\n    89\t    event DrawRequested(\n    90\t        uint256 indexed requestId,\n    91\t        address indexed requester,\n    92\t        uint256 fee,\n    93\t        uint256 excessReturned,\n    94\t        uint256 drawRequestedAt,\n    95\t        uint256 callbackDeadline\n    96\t    );\n    97\t\n    98\t    /// @notice Emitted when an authenticated, ABI-decodable callback cannot resolve the raffle.\n    99\t    /// @param receivedRequestId Request ID supplied by the wrapper callback.\n   100\t    /// @param expectedRequestId Request ID currently recorded by the raffle, or zero before request persistence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":true,\"stub_explanation\":\"No supported vulnerability found. Settlement validates and records the winning ticket once. Raffle.sol:316–317 rejects any differing uint256 ticket ID before ownership lookup, claim consumption, or external calls. The stated actor cannot overwrite the settled winner or bypass this comparison.\",\"results\":[]}"}}
